Operator change: Line Art (was 12) and Smooth (was 24) now remove lone
1-px ink specks only, as potrace's default speck size of 2 does. Small
text keeps the dot on its i, and Smooth keeps whole letters in 16 px text.
Sharp, Centerline and Edge Detection keep their values, and the control
still takes larger values for art that needs more cleanup.

Measured against 85ee406 with the whole package applied: Line Art and
Smooth trace 25 of 25 shapes on the audit's sans 32 px, serif 32 px,
noisy 32 px and sans 16 px text (were 24, and Smooth 22 on 16 px text);
IoU rises in all eight, and the noisy text gains no specks. On the dragon
the default adds 657 Line Art and 443 Smooth outlines on top of the
connectivity and crack changes (3,468 and 3,691 in total, from 1,804 and
1,713); the added marks are darker than the cut. On the Arch House logo
Line Art gains five pale spots (1 to 19 px², darkest pixels luma 115 to
234) that the local-contrast detail pass finds in light shading; speck
removal at 12 used to hide them.

Updated expectation, the intended fix: the Centerline connectivity test
now expects Line Art to keep both diagonals (23 ink pixels) and drop only
the lone speck. TraceSettingsControls.semantic.test.tsx's speck test
assumed the old default; the next commit adapts it.

